> String.trim

    String.trim : (String) -> String

Without leading and trailing whitespace.

Examples

    String.trim("  hi\n")
    // => "hi"
> no command :zz; :help lists them
> :b is :bindings or :browse
> :f is :faults or :forget
> :type takes an expression
> no module Nope is in scope
> aaaa is not a module name: each segment of one begins with a capital letter, as in Http.Parser
> no module Nope under the source root or on the load path
> List is the standard library's, in scope from the start
> :reload takes no argument
> no documentation for Nope.nope
